<title>UK: Kingfisher buys Dutch electrical retailer.</title>
<headline>Kingfisher buys Dutch electrical retailer.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>British retailer Kingfisher Plc said on Tuesday it had bought Dutch eletrical retailer BCC Holding B.V. for 33.6 million stg in cash.  </p>
<p>BCC has 17 stores in the Amsterdam and Rotterdam area. It had turnover of 77.8 million stg in the year to March 31, 1997.</p>
<p>Philippe Frances, chief executive of Kingfisher Electrical retailing Ltd, said, &quot;This acquisition carries forward one strand of our strategy for growth in Europe. We are now operating in France, the UK, Belgium and Holland.&quot;</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
